    "question": {
      ":question/id": "971064cb-49d8-55b6-9f9f-830554f91079",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 7 & 6 \\\\ 4 & 3 & 4 \\\\ -7 & 7 & 3 \\\\ -8 & -4 & -9\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & -4 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $4\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 4$ row vector. \n\nThere are $4$ columns in $S$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $S$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $4$ columns in $R$ and $1$ row in $S.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $S,$ the matrices $R$ and $S$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times 4}{\\times }_{\\ne }{S}_{1\\times 4}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $4$ columns in $R$ and $4$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{4}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{4}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe products $SP$ and $RP$ are well defined. The product $RS$ is undefined.",
