  {
    "knowledge_point": {
      "db_id": 17592186100869,
      "id": "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140",
      "title": "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "e9c0bef3-3fdb-5cff-a06b-04ae0d35cb30",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -6 & -9 \\\\ -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ -7 & 1 & -6 \\\\ -4 & 4 & -1 \\\\ -4 & -8 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 2 & -6 & -3 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$S=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $P,R,$ and $S?$\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $P$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, $R$ is a $1\\times 5$ row vector, and $S$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector.\n\nThere are $2$ columns in $S$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $S$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $S$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{S}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ columns in $R$ and $5$ rows in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $R$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $R$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{R}_{1\\times \\boxed{\\text{5}}}{\\times }_{\u2713}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{5}}\\times 3}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there are $3$ columns in $P$ and $1$ row in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $P$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{5\\times 3}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{1\\times 5}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nThe product $RP$ is well defined. The products $SR$ and $PR$ are undefined.",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "637cd709-9392-533b-ac88-16f65347e597",
          ":answer-field/key": "The product $SR$ is well defined.",
